\nP: d7-d5 is also good, but after exd5 Qxd5, Nc6 attacks the queen, but Qa5 or Qd6 leads to positions where Black's queen can be harassed. I prefer developing a piece first.\n\nBetween Nf6 and d5, Nf6 is slightly more flexible and keeps more tension.\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6"}
